# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

The browser's Back, and Android's back gesture, close the topmost open overlay before they leave the screen. That covers:
- the inspect, face-down and pile sheets, and the card detail;
- the command menu;
- the settings panel;
- the friends panel, a conversation and the challenge dialog;
- the Concede and "Leave this game?" confirms, where Back means "Keep playing".

One Back closes one overlay, newest first, and leaves the address and the screen as they were.

Where the browser has `CloseWatcher`, the overlay uses it. Elsewhere the client keeps one history entry of its own:
- it never piles up;
- Forward never reopens what it closed;
- it never reaches R1754000's leave guard.

A `Prompt`, a play still being built and the mulligan are not overlays, so with one of them on top, Back works as it does today. The ruling is R2127000.

## Files to touch

| File | Kind | What |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `apps/web/src/net/backLayers.ts` | new | the layer stack, `useBackLayer`, `popBackLayer`, `moveOverBackEntry` |
| `apps/web/src/net/navigate.ts` | change | `onPop` asks `popBackLayer` first; `go` calls `moveOverBackEntry` |
| `apps/web/src/cards/inspect/store.ts` | change | `useModalOverlay`: `useBackLayer(close)`, `preventDefault` on Escape |
| `apps/web/src/together/modalKeys.ts` | change | `useModalKeys`: `useBackLayer(onClose)` |
| `apps/web/src/settings/SettingsPanel.tsx` | change | `useBackLayer(onClose)`, `preventDefault` on Escape |
| `apps/web/src/game/ConfirmConcede.tsx` | change | `useBackLayer(onCancel)` |
| `apps/web/src/practice/PracticeLeave.tsx` | change | `useBackLayer(onStay)`, `preventDefault` on Escape |
| `apps/web/src/together/ChatPanel.tsx` | change | `useBackLayer(onClose)`, `preventDefault` on Escape |
| `apps/web/src/test/history.ts` | new | `HISTORY_TURNS`, `pressBack`, `pressForward` |
| `apps/web/src/net/backLayers.test.tsx` | new | the mechanism, the leave guard, `CloseWatcher`, the sheets, `PracticeLeave` |
| `apps/web/src/game/ConfirmConcede.test.tsx` | change | concede; a Prompt or the mulligan on top |
| `apps/web/src/routes/command-menu.test.tsx` | change | the command menu |
| `apps/web/src/test/ux/settings.test.tsx` | change | the settings panel |
| `apps/web/src/together/FriendsButton.test.tsx` | change | the friends panel and the challenge dialog |
| `apps/web/src/together/ChatPanel.test.tsx` | change | a conversation |
| `spec/rulings/R2127000.md` | new | the ruling |
| `spec/pending/2127.md` | new | its §11 paragraph |
| `spec/10-engine-guide.md` | change | one §10.10 paragraph |
| `apps/web/README.md` | change | one paragraph, the concede sentence, the `src/test/` list |

Do not touch:
- `crates/`, `e2e/`, `Prompt.tsx`, `Game.tsx` or `CommandMenu.tsx`;
- `spec/11-rulings.md` or `spec/INDEX.md`;
- any config or manifest;
- `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/` or `bot/`.

Never run `cargo jackioh spec index`.

What governs this: SPEC §10.10 and §10.6, and rulings R1754000, R2117000, R2118000 and R2121000.

## Steps

1. **Write `spec/rulings/R2127000.md`.** Copy the front matter layout of `R2121000.md`:
   - `id: R2127000`
   - `title: "Back closes the topmost sheet or dialog before it leaves the screen (issue #2127)"`
   - `cards: "§10.10, §10.6, R313, R370, R1754000, R2117000, R2118000, R2121000, issue #2036, issue #2127"`
   - `proven_in`: the six test files listed under **Tests**.

   The body has these paragraphs, in this order:
   - **Which.** The Goal's list, plus every dialog built on the same two modal hooks: the stack sheet, hero inspect and the pack scene. Each closes through its own close, so the focus goes back.
   - **Never by Back.** A prompt, a play being built and the mulligan ([[§10.6]]; Hearthstone semantics, as [[R2121000]] has it).
     - The hotseat hand-over is a button and draws no screen.
     - Inline questions and the result dialogs are unchanged.
     - The pack scene ignores Back while its open request is out.
   - **How.**
     - Where `CloseWatcher` exists, the top overlay holds one.
     - Otherwise the first overlay pushes one history entry that copies the address, and a Back off it closes the top overlay.
     - An overlay closed some other way leaves that entry spent. The next overlay reuses it, a move takes its place, Back steps on past it, and Forward onto it steps back.
   - **Leave guard.** Closing an overlay never reaches [[R1754000]] or a view transition ([[R2117000]]).
   - **Rejected.** One entry per overlay. Calling `history.back()` on every close, which races a move made in the same click. Treating every `role="dialog"` as an overlay.
   - End with "Presentation only (CLAUDE.md rule 7)."

2. **Write `spec/pending/2127.md`.** One paragraph, shaped like `2117.md`: `**[[R2127000]] Back closes the topmost sheet or dialog before it leaves the screen (issue #2127, part of #2036, 2026-10-29)**: …`. End it with "It takes R2127000, the first number of issue #2127's block, and edits [[§10.10]]."

3. **Edit `spec/10-engine-guide.md`.** After the R2117000 paragraph (the last one before `### 10.11`), add two sentences linking [[R2127000]]: Back closes the topmost sheet or dialog first, and never a prompt, a play being built or the mulligan. End with "Presentation only."

4. **Create `apps/web/src/net/backLayers.ts`.**
   - Start it with a header comment of about six lines summing up the ruling's **How**.
   - Give each export a `/** R2127000: … */` doc comment.
   - Format it in prettier style.
   - Put no top-level `window` access in it, because Vite's config loader imports `navigate.ts`.

   The code:
   ```ts
