# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

The 7m 7s job #2323 reports ran before the fix. Run 40794344814 tested `a1382fc` (pushed 00:28 UTC on 2026-10-29). #2323 was claimed at 02:17:38 UTC, so that job started by 02:10:31, before #2288 (68edaae1a, merged 02:11:04) split `rust (test server)` into four groups (`server`, `server api`, `server practice`, `server practice rulings`). `git show a1382fc:.github/workflows/ci.yml` still has the single `test: -p jackioh-server` group. Main has had the split since then.

The split still has thin headroom. On a 4-core GitHub runner (AMD EPYC 7763, the same as CI's), with CI's `CARGO_PROFILE_TEST_DEBUG=0` and the workspace crates compiled fresh as CI compiles them, compile plus run (setup not included) is:

- `server`: 160 + 100 s
- `server api`: 160 + 61 s
- `server practice`: 187 + 90 s
- `server practice rulings`: 187 + 97 s

One test is half of `server`'s run: `bots::seat::r2214000_a_strength_zero_miss_makes_far_fewer_beginners_mistakes_than_random`. It plays 20 random games one after another (52 s), and it is the last test the binary waits on. It came in with #2294 (22:16 UTC on Oct 28), which was likely after #2288 took its measurements.

Done means:
- That test plays its 20 games side by side, one scoped thread each.
- Its assertions and the counts it prints are unchanged.
- The `server` group's binary run drops from about 96 s to about 76 s.
- There is no `ci.yml` change.
- The PR closes #2323.

## Files to touch

